{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019HLfAndP9P2VX3127ENehy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand what needs to be done.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development using Unix utilities as a test bed. It derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations using AI, and verifies parity via differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: \n- `cmd/` - one package per utility\n- `pkg/testutils/` - differential testing harness\n- `pkg/sys/` - syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` - output formatting\n- `pkg/hashutil/` - hash utility shared code\n\n\n- `pkg/sizeparse/` - size parsing\n- `pkg/encutil/` - encoding utility shared code\n- `magefiles/` - build automation\n- `docs/` - specifications\n\n**Current Implementation State**: Looking at the code status, several utilities and packages haven't been started yet—format and testutils have contracts but no implementation, while cat, nproc, ls, and logname are all pending work across different release versions.\n\nScanning through the remaining releases, there's a substantial backlog of unstarted items spanning from echo and tac in 05.0 through the entire 11.0 release, including utilities like sort, mv, sleep, and various checksum and encoding tools that need implementation. I'm scanning through the requirement states for various SRDs to identify which ones are fully ready versus partially complete. Most of these checksums and file utilities show all requirements met, though a few like srd092-mkfifo appear to be still in progress. I'm seeing that the requirement_states list only includes SRDs with requirements in ready state, so those earlier releases might have their requirements already satisfied even though they're not listed here. Let me trace back through the roadmap to find which release is actually incomplete—I need