{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019HLfAndP9P2VX3127ENehy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go from formal specifications, verifying parity via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<utility>/` holds per-utility implementations with differential tests; `pkg/testutils/` provides the test harness; `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls; `pkg/format/` handles output formatting; `pkg/hashutil/` provides shared checksum logic; `docs/specs/` contains SRDs, use cases, and test suites.\n\n**Current state**: Generation run 44 is in progress. Many utilities across releases 00.0-08.1 have been implemented. The `requirement_states` field shows which requirements are still \"ready\" for new tasks.\n\n**Earliest incomplete release with ready requirements**: **09.0** (sha224sum, sha384sum, b2sum, cksum, sum). For sha224sum, R1/R2 were handled by earlier tasks in this run — only R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3 remain. For sha384sum, all 12 requirements are ready.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 09.0 is the earliest with ready R-items. sha224sum has 5 ready requirements (closest to completion). sha384sum has 12. I'll finish sha224sum (2 tasks) and start sha384sum (2 tasks) to fill the 4-task budget.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\nAssuming default weight 1 for all requirements (requirements.yaml not available in project_context):\n\n- Task 0: srd074 R3.1(w=1) + R3.2(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) = 4 — at limit\n- Task 1: srd074 R4.3(w=1) = 1 — within limit\n- Task 2: srd075 R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 — at limit\n- Task 3: srd075 R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) + R3.1(w=1) = 4 — at limit\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/sha224sum: implement srd074 R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd074-sha224sum.yaml (requirements R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2)\n      - pkg/hashutil/ (shared checksum library -- HashConfig, DigestFiles, VerifyChecksums, FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ParseChecksumLine)\n      - cmd/sha224sum/main.go (existing implementation from earlier tasks covering R1/R2 -- extend this file)\n      - cmd/md5sum/main.go (reference implementation of a checksum utility using pkg/hashutil, if it exists)\n      - cmd/sha256sum/main.go (reference implementation of a checksum utility using pkg/hashutil, if it exists)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/sha224sum/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd074 R3.1, R3.2, R4.1, R4.2 to existing sha224sum implementation\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd074 R3.1 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and implement it in cmd/sha224sum/main.go\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd074 R3.2 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and implement it in cmd/sha224sum/main.go\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd074 R4.1 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and implement it in cmd/sha224sum/main.go\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd074 R4.2 -- read the SRD for the exact requirement text and implement it in cmd/sha224sum/main.go\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/hashutil.HashConfig with crypto/sha256.New224 as the hash constructor and DigestLen 28 (224 bits / 8)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Delegate file hashing to pkg/hashutil.DigestFiles and checksum verification to pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums -- do not reimplement checksum logic in cmd/\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Follow the same structure as cmd/md5sum or cmd/sha256sum if they exist -- sha224sum is a thin wrapper around pkg/hashutil with SHA-224 configuration\"\n      - i